    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "NEW TO THE MARKET\r\n\r\nPrime c.0.5 Acre Mature Tree-Lined Site\r\n\r\nLisacul, Co. Roscommon\r\n\r\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers are delighted to present this attractive c.0.5 acre mature tree-lined site located just outside Lisacul Village in a peaceful countryside setting.\r\n\r\nThis excellent roadside site comprises dry, level ground and offers an ideal opportunity for those seeking to build a family home in a highly convenient location, subject to the necessary planning permission being obtained.\r\n\r\nThe site benefits from mature trees along its boundaries, creating privacy and character while retaining excellent accessibility to surrounding towns and amenities.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n\r\n• Prime c.0.5 acre roadside site\r\n• Mature tree-lined boundaries\r\n• Dry, level ground ideal for construction\r\n• Water passing the property\r\n• ESB passing the property\r\n• Quiet countryside setting\r\n• Excellent road frontage and accessibility\r\n• Ideal family home site subject to planning permission\r\n\r\nLocation Highlights\r\n\r\n• Close to Lisacul Village\r\n• Walking distance to Church, National School and Community Centre\r\n• Approx. 5 minutes to Loughglynn\r\n• Approx. 10 minutes to Ballaghaderreen\r\n• Approx. 15 minutes to Castlerea\r\n• Approx. 25 minutes to Ireland West Airport Knock\r\n• Convenient to all local amenities and services\r\n\r\nThis site offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a quality building site in a sought-after rural location with excellent connectivity.\r\n\r\nViewing comes highly recommended and is strictly by appointment with the sole selling agent.\r\n\r\nSole Agent\r\n\r\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers\r\nMIPAV MMCEPI\r\nPSRA Licence No. 002031\r\n\r\n086 2130723 | 094 9362216\r\n\r\nEverything we touch turns to SOLD\r\n\r\nDisclaimer\r\n\r\nThese particulars are issued for guidance only and do not form part of any contract. Intending purchasers should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of all information provided."
      },
